let __v_4265 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[\"A promise that moves every time is a pattern, not a date. Ask for the day itself, in a message, so there is something written down - which day, and put it in the calendar - and believe the answer rather than the intention. What is it they keep putting off?\",\"Stop asking whether it will happen and ask what has happened: one small thing this week, in writing. A day that slips again is the answer, and it is better to know that before you count on it. What have you been counting on?\",\"Say it once, plainly, and ask which day they mean: a promise that never gets a day is the thing worth testing, and testing it is fairer than deciding what they are like. What would change for you if it actually happened?\"]}")?;
